title: Fiscal Policy
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet
on-arrival: fiscal_policy_timer += 6; month_actions += 1
view-if: spd_in_government = 1 and finance_minister_party = "SPD" and fiscal_policy_timer = 0
card-image: img/portraits/HilferdingRudolf.jpg
go-to: fiscal_menu

@fiscal_menu
on-arrival: dissent_dampener = (1 - dissent); progressivity_gap = upper_tax_rates - lower_tax_rates;

Upper-income tax rates: [+ upper_tax_rates : taxation +]

Middle-income tax rates: [+ middle_tax_rates: taxation +]

Lower-income tax rates: [+ lower_tax_rates : taxation +]

- @raise_rich: Increase taxes on the rich.
- @raise_middle: Increase taxes on the middle class.
- @raise_poor
- @overall_menu: Change taxes broadly across brackets.
- @cut_rich
- @cut_middle
- @cut_poor
- @raise_progressive: Make the tax system more progressive by raising taxes on the rich and cutting them for the poor.
- @regressive
- @tariffs
- @root: Do not change the tax system.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@raise_progressive
subtitle: This does not change overall revenue. [? if lower_tax_rates < -5 : Lower-class tax rates are too low to cut anymore. ?] [? if upper_tax_rates > 5 : Upper-class tax rates are too high to increase. ?]
choose-if: lower_tax_rates >= -5 and upper_tax_rates <= 5
on-arrival: workers_spd += 6*(1-dissent); old_middle_spd -= 4; new_middle_spd -= 4; coalition_dissent += 1 if in_grand_coalition; dvp_relation -= 4; finance_goal_completed += 1; upper_tax_rates += 1; lower_tax_rates -= 1; new_middle_spd -= 2 if upper_tax_rates > 1; old_middle_spd -= 2 if upper_tax_rates > 1; demand_impulse += 0.1; supply_impulse -= 0.04; capital_strike_progress += 1; capital_strike_progress += 1 if upper_tax_rates > 1; capital_strike_progress += 1 if upper_tax_rates > 3;

Making the tax system more progressive is popular among our base, but it upsets our bourgeois coalition partners, as well as our minimal number of bourgeois voters. Middle-income rates are left unchanged, positioning the middle class between the two poles of this reform.

@raise_rich
subtitle: +2 budget
unavailable-subtitle: Tax rates are already too high.
choose-if: upper_tax_rates <= 5
on-arrival: workers_spd += 4*(1-dissent); old_middle_spd -= 4; new_middle_spd -= 4; coalition_dissent += 1 if in_grand_coalition; coalition_dissent += 1 if capital_strike_progress >= 5; dvp_relation -= 4; left_dissent -= 3; labor_dissent -= 3; finance_goal_completed += 1; upper_tax_rates += 1; budget += 2; new_middle_spd -= 2 if upper_tax_rates > 1; old_middle_spd -= 2 if upper_tax_rates > 1; demand_impulse += 0.05; supply_impulse -= 0.06; price_pressure -= 0.1; capital_strike_progress += 1; capital_strike_progress += 1 if upper_tax_rates > 1; capital_strike_progress += 1 if upper_tax_rates > 3; dvp_dissent += 2; wp_dissent += 3

Raising taxes on the rich is popular among our base, but it alienates the bourgeoisie. Increasing taxes also decreases economic demand, which may lead to more unemployment.

@raise_middle
title: Increase taxes on the middle class.
subtitle: +2 budget
unavailable-subtitle: Tax rates are already too high.
choose-if: middle_tax_rates <= 5
on-arrival: new_middle_spd -= 6; old_middle_spd -= 2; workers_spd += 1*(1-dissent); ddp_relation -= 3; finance_goal_completed += 1; middle_tax_rates += 1; budget += 2; new_middle_spd -= 3 if middle_tax_rates > 1; demand_impulse += 0.04; supply_impulse -= 0.05; price_pressure -= 0.08; capital_strike_progress += 1 if middle_tax_rates > 3;

Raising taxes on the middle class alienates a group we rely on for swing support, though it does little to upset the working class or the wealthy directly.

@raise_poor
title: Raise consumption taxes, which disproportionately affect the poor.
subtitle: +2 budget
unavailable-subtitle: Tax rates are already too high.
choose-if: lower_tax_rates <= 5
on-arrival: budget += 2; workers_spd -= 4; kpd_coalition_dissent += 1; labor_dissent += 3; left_dissent += 3; lower_tax_rates += 1; workers_spd -= 5 if lower_tax_rates >= 2; demand_impulse -= 0.15; price_pressure -= 0.08; demand_impulse -= 0.1 if lower_tax_rates >= 2; general_strike_progress += lower_tax_rates

We have raised taxes for the poor and working class. This hurts our support among the workers.

@cut_rich
title: Cut income taxes for the rich.
subtitle: -2 budget
unavailable-subtitle: -2 budget - [? if upper_tax_rates < -5: Tax rates are already too low. ?]
choose-if: budget >= 2 and upper_tax_rates >= -5
on-arrival: budget -= 2; new_middle_spd += 5*(1-dissent); old_middle_spd += 4*(1-dissent); dvp_relation += 4*(1-dissent); z_relation += 4*(1-dissent); labor_dissent += 3; left_dissent += 3; upper_tax_rates -= 1; capital_strike_progress -= 1 if upper_tax_rates < 0; demand_impulse += 0.1; supply_impulse += 0.25; price_pressure += 0.1;

We have reduced income and property taxes for the rich and middle class. The bourgeois parties approve of this orthodox economic course.

@cut_middle
title: Cut taxes for the middle class.
subtitle: -2 budget
unavailable-subtitle: -2 budget - [? if middle_tax_rates < -5: Tax rates are already too low. ?]
choose-if: budget >= 2 and middle_tax_rates >= -5
on-arrival: budget -= 2; new_middle_spd += 6*(1-dissent); old_middle_spd += 2*(1-dissent); ddp_relation += 3*(1-dissent); middle_tax_rates -= 1; demand_impulse += 0.2; price_pressure += 0.1;

Tax cuts targeted at the middle class win favor with white-collar workers and professionals.

@cut_poor
title: Cut consumption taxes for the poor.
subtitle: -2 budget
unavailable-subtitle: -2 budget - [? if lower_tax_rates < -5: Tax rates are already too low. ?]
choose-if: budget >= 2 and lower_tax_rates >= -5
on-arrival: budget -= 2; workers_spd += 5*(1-dissent); finance_goal_completed += 1; labor_dissent -= 3; left_dissent -= 3; lower_tax_rates -= 1; demand_impulse += 0.35; price_pressure += 0.15; general_strike_progress -= 2

Our tax cuts disproportionately benefit the poor and working class.

@overall_menu
title: Adjust taxes broadly across multiple brackets.

- @raise_upper_middle: Raise taxes on upper and middle incomes.
- @raise_middle_lower: Raise taxes on middle and lower incomes.
- @raise_lower_upper: Raise taxes on lower and upper incomes.
- @raise_all_three: Raise taxes across all income brackets.
- @cut_upper_middle: Cut taxes on upper and middle incomes.
- @cut_middle_lower: Cut taxes on middle and lower incomes.
- @cut_lower_upper: Cut taxes on lower and upper incomes.
- @cut_all_three: Cut taxes across all income brackets.
- @fiscal_menu: Back.
- @easy_discard

@raise_upper_middle
title: Raise taxes on upper and middle incomes.
subtitle: +3 budget
unavailable-subtitle: Tax rates are already too high.
choose-if: upper_tax_rates <= 5 and middle_tax_rates <= 5
on-arrival: budget += 3; workers_spd += 2*(1-dissent); new_middle_spd -= 6; old_middle_spd -= 3; coalition_dissent += 1 if in_grand_coalition; dvp_relation -= 3; ddp_relation -= 3; finance_goal_completed += 1; upper_tax_rates += 1; middle_tax_rates += 1; new_middle_spd -= 2 if upper_tax_rates > 1; old_middle_spd -= 1 if upper_tax_rates > 1; demand_impulse += 0.03; supply_impulse -= 0.06; price_pressure -= 0.06; capital_strike_progress += 1; capital_strike_progress += 1 if upper_tax_rates > 1;

We have raised taxes on the wealthy and the middle class, sparing the working poor. Both the bourgeoisie and white-collar professionals are unhappy with this course.

@raise_middle_lower
title: Raise taxes on middle and lower incomes.
subtitle: +3 budget
unavailable-subtitle: Tax rates are already too high.
choose-if: middle_tax_rates <= 5 and lower_tax_rates <= 5
on-arrival: budget += 3; new_middle_spd -= 5; old_middle_spd -= 2; workers_spd -= 4; kpd_coalition_dissent += 1; labor_dissent += 2; left_dissent += 2; ddp_relation -= 2; middle_tax_rates += 1; lower_tax_rates += 1; workers_spd -= 4 if lower_tax_rates > 1; new_middle_spd -= 2 if middle_tax_rates > 1; demand_impulse -= 0.1; supply_impulse -= 0.06; price_pressure -= 0.15; general_strike_progress += lower_tax_rates;

Raising taxes on the middle and working class spares the wealthy, drawing criticism that the burden falls unevenly on those least able to bear it.

@raise_lower_upper
title: Raise taxes on lower and upper incomes.
subtitle: +3 budget
unavailable-subtitle: Tax rates are already too high.
choose-if: lower_tax_rates <= 5 and upper_tax_rates <= 5
on-arrival: budget += 3; workers_spd -= 3; new_middle_spd += 1*(1-dissent); coalition_dissent += 1 if in_grand_coalition; dvp_relation -= 3; kpd_coalition_dissent += 1; labor_dissent += 2; left_dissent += 1; lower_tax_rates += 1; upper_tax_rates += 1; workers_spd -= 4 if lower_tax_rates > 1; new_middle_spd -= 1 if upper_tax_rates > 1; demand_impulse -= 0.08; supply_impulse -= 0.08; price_pressure -= 0.15; general_strike_progress += lower_tax_rates; capital_strike_progress += 1 if upper_tax_rates > 1;

We tax the rich and poor alike, leaving the middle class untouched — an unusual pairing that satisfies almost no one ideologically, but the middle class approves of being left out of it.

@raise_all_three
title: Raise taxes across all income brackets.
subtitle: +4 budget
unavailable-subtitle: Tax rates are already too high.
choose-if: upper_tax_rates <= 5 and middle_tax_rates <= 5 and lower_tax_rates <= 5
on-arrival: budget += 4; new_middle_spd -= 5; old_middle_spd -= 4; workers_spd -= 4; kpd_coalition_dissent += 1; lower_tax_rates += 1; middle_tax_rates += 1; upper_tax_rates += 1; workers_spd -= 5 if lower_tax_rates > 1; new_middle_spd -= 3 if middle_tax_rates > 1; new_middle_spd -= 2 if upper_tax_rates > 1; old_middle_spd -= 2 if upper_tax_rates > 1; capital_strike_progress += 1 if upper_tax_rates > 1; capital_strike_progress += 1 if upper_tax_rates > 2; demand_impulse -= 0.15; supply_impulse -= 0.1; price_pressure -= 0.28; general_strike_progress += 1;

Raising taxes across every bracket hurts our support broadly. [? if in_grand_coalition or in_weimar_coalition : Our coalition partners frame this as "shared sacrifice," softening some of the backlash. ?] Increasing taxes this broadly also risks a meaningful contraction in economic demand.

@cut_upper_middle
title: Cut taxes on upper and middle incomes.
subtitle: -3 budget
unavailable-subtitle: -3 budget - [? if upper_tax_rates < -5 or middle_tax_rates < -5 : Tax rates are already too low. ?]
choose-if: budget >= 3 and upper_tax_rates >= -5 and middle_tax_rates >= -5
on-arrival: budget -= 3; new_middle_spd += 7*(1-dissent); old_middle_spd += 3*(1-dissent); dvp_relation += 4*(1-dissent); ddp_relation += 4*(1-dissent); z_relation += 3*(1-dissent); upper_tax_rates -= 1; middle_tax_rates -= 1; capital_strike_progress -= 1 if upper_tax_rates < 0; demand_impulse += 0.2; supply_impulse += 0.2; price_pressure += 0.2;

Cutting taxes on the wealthy and the middle class pleases both the bourgeoisie and professionals, while leaving working-class taxation untouched.

@cut_middle_lower
title: Cut taxes on middle and lower incomes.
subtitle: -3 budget
unavailable-subtitle: -3 budget - [? if middle_tax_rates < -5 or lower_tax_rates < -5: Tax rates are already too low. ?]
choose-if: budget >= 3 and middle_tax_rates >= -5 and lower_tax_rates >= -5
on-arrival: budget -= 3; new_middle_spd += 6*(1-dissent); old_middle_spd += 1*(1-dissent); workers_spd += 4*(1-dissent); finance_goal_completed += 1; labor_dissent -= 2; left_dissent -= 2; ddp_relation += 3*(1-dissent); middle_tax_rates -= 1; lower_tax_rates -= 1; demand_impulse += 0.3; price_pressure += 0.2; general_strike_progress -= 2;

Our tax cuts benefit the middle and working classes together, a combination that plays well with the broad center-left of our coalition.

@cut_lower_upper
title: Cut taxes on lower and upper incomes.
subtitle: -3 budget
unavailable-subtitle: -3 budget - [? if lower_tax_rates < -5 or upper_tax_rates < -5: Tax rates are already too low. ?]
choose-if: budget >= 3 and lower_tax_rates >= -5 and upper_tax_rates >= -5
on-arrival: budget -= 3; workers_spd += 4*(1-dissent); new_middle_spd -= 1; dvp_relation += 3*(1-dissent); z_relation += 2*(1-dissent); labor_dissent -= 1; left_dissent -= 1; lower_tax_rates -= 1; upper_tax_rates -= 1; capital_strike_progress -= 1 if upper_tax_rates < 0; demand_impulse += 0.25; supply_impulse += 0.15; price_pressure += 0.2; general_strike_progress -= 2;

We cut taxes for the rich and poor alike, leaving the middle class to shoulder a relatively larger share. This odd pairing puzzles commentators but delivers real relief to both ends of the income spectrum.

@cut_all_three
title: Cut taxes across all income brackets.
subtitle: -4 budget
unavailable-subtitle: -4 budget - [? if upper_tax_rates < -5 or middle_tax_rates < -5 or lower_tax_rates < -5 : Tax rates are already too low. ?]
choose-if: budget >= 4 and upper_tax_rates >= -5 and middle_tax_rates >= -5 and lower_tax_rates >= -5
on-arrival: budget -= 4; new_middle_spd += 7*(1-dissent); old_middle_spd += 5*(1-dissent); workers_spd += 3*(1-dissent); dvp_relation += 5*(1-dissent); ddp_relation += 4*(1-dissent); z_relation += 5*(1-dissent); upper_tax_rates -= 1; middle_tax_rates -= 1; lower_tax_rates -= 1; capital_strike_progress -= 1 if upper_tax_rates < 0; demand_impulse += 0.4; supply_impulse += 0.22; price_pressure += 0.35; general_strike_progress -= 1;

Cutting taxes across every bracket is broadly popular and reassures markets and coalition partners alike, though it comes at real cost to the treasury.

@regressive
title: Lower taxes on the rich, while increasing consumption taxes (which affect the working class more).
subtitle: This does not change overall revenue. [? if upper_tax_rates < -5 : Rich tax rates are too low to cut anymore. ?] [? if lower_tax_rates > 5 : Lower-class tax rates are too high to increase. ?]
choose-if: lower_tax_rates <= 5 and upper_tax_rates >= -5
on-arrival: workers_spd -= 6; new_middle_spd += 5*(1-dissent); old_middle_spd += 5*(1-dissent); dvp_relation += 5; z_relation += 4; coalition_dissent -= 1 if in_grand_coalition and coalition_dissent > 0; kpd_coalition_dissent += 1; labor_dissent += 5; left_dissent += 5; upper_tax_rates -= 1; lower_tax_rates += 1; workers_spd -= 5 if lower_tax_rates >= 2; capital_strike_progress -= 1 if upper_tax_rates < 0; demand_impulse -= 0.1; supply_impulse += 0.08; general_strike_progress += lower_tax_rates

Our regressive taxation policy benefits the rich while hurting the poor and working-class. Middle-income rates are left unchanged, positioned between the two extremes of this reform. Our bourgeois coalition partners approve of this orthodox economic course.

@tariffs
title: Change tariffs instead.

Tariffs, or taxes on international imports, are another way to finance our government.

Historically, socialists have been in favor of free trade and a low-tariff regime. Workers in export-oriented industries benefit from free trade, and they also benefit from lower prices for imported necessities. Do the present economic circumstances change these calculations?

Current tariff level: [+ tariffs : taxation +]

- @raise_tariffs
- @lower_tariffs
- @fiscal_menu: Change domestic taxes instead of tariffs.
- @root: Do not change tariffs or taxes.
- @easy_discard

@raise_tariffs
title: Raise tariffs on imports.
subtitle: +2 budget. Other countries will retaliate by increasing tariffs of their own. [? if tariffs > 5 : Further increases in tariffs will not raise revenue, as we have already nearly reached econonmic autarky. ?]
choose-if: tariffs <= 5
on-arrival: tariffs += 1; budget += 2; workers_spd -= 5; unemployed_spd -= 5; rural_spd += 4*(1-dissent); old_middle_spd += 3*(1-dissent); ddp_relation -= 5; dvp_relation -= 2; britain_relation -= 1; france_relation -= 2; poland_relation -= 1; reparations_negotiation -= 2; eu_progress -= 1 if eu_progress > 0; peoples_party_support += 1; price_pressure += 0.3; supply_impulse -= 0.15; demand_impulse -= 0.12; capital_strike_progress += 1 if tariffs >= 3;

Increasing tariffs leads to higher prices for basic goods, increasing inflation and hurting consumption among the working class. Retaliatory tariffs reduce the competitiveness of German exports, raising unemployment among workers. They also lead to an atmosphere of international suspicion, reducing our ability to negotiate with other countries.

On the other hand, agricultural producers and some small businesses benefit from higher tariffs, as farmers can now command higher prices for grain, and formerly uncompetitive businesses are now able to function.

@lower_tariffs
title: Lower tariffs on imports.
choose-if: budget >= 2 and tariffs > -5
subtitle: -2 budget. [? if tariffs <= -5 : There are no tariffs left to cut. ?]
on-arrival: tariffs -= 1; budget -= 2; workers_spd += 4*(1-dissent); unemployed_spd += 4*(1-dissent); rural_spd -= 5; old_middle_spd -= 3; britain_relation += 1; france_relation += 1; poland_relation += 1; eu_progress += 1 if eu_progress > 0; price_pressure -= 0.25; supply_impulse += 0.18; demand_impulse += 0.12;

Lowering tariffs helps workers and the urban poor by reducing prices for basic necessities. In addition, other countries are pleased by lower tariffs, and are more willing to negotiate on many issues.

Farmers are hurt by this policy, as cheap imported grain leads to ruin for some small producers. In general, cheap imports are detrimental for small-scale industries aimed at the domestic market.
